{% doc %}
  Renders an inline SVG icon.

  Icons are inlined rather than sprited or served as files, for three reasons:
  they inherit `currentColor` so a scheme change recolours them for free, there
  is no extra request on a store where the header alone needs five of them, and
  no icon can ever fail to load and leave an empty box in the navigation.

  Every icon is `aria-hidden` and `focusable="false"`. An icon never carries the
  accessible name — the button around it does, through a translated
  `aria-label` or visually hidden text. An icon that labels itself produces
  duplicate announcements as soon as the button has text too.

  @param {string} icon - Icon name. See the list below.
  @param {string} [class] - Extra classes
  @param {number} [size] - Pixel size. Defaults to 16, applied as an inline custom property so CSS can still override it.

  Available: account, arrow-left, arrow-right, atom, bag, bolt, brain, capsule,
  cart, cells, chat, check, chevron-down, chevron-left, chevron-right,
  chevron-up, clock, close, compare, compound, copy, droplet, edit, external,
  filter, filter-off, grid, heart, heart-filled, info, leaf, list, loader,
  location, lock, mail, menu, minus, molecule, moon, note, pause, phone, play,
  plus, pulse, quote, refresh, search, share, sort, sparkle, star, star-half,
  sun, tag, trash, truck, warning, zoom-in

  An unknown name renders an empty `<svg>` — see the `else` at the end of the
  case. That is deliberate (a placeholder glyph in production is worse than a
  missing decoration) and it fails silently, so a block whose icon setting can
  hold a name this list does not have should check it before rendering rather
  than pass it straight through. `blocks/_product-bundle-category.liquid` has
  the worked example and the reason.

  Brand marks: bluesky, facebook, instagram, linkedin, pinterest, snapchat,
  threads, tiktok, tumblr, vimeo, x, youtube

  A `{% comment %}` inside the element below must not spell the svg tag out in
  angle brackets. Theme Check parses comment bodies as HTML, an opening svg tag
  there starts a raw node, and the one closing tag at the end of the file goes
  to that node instead — so the real element never closes and the whole file
  fails to parse. Write "the `svg` element" instead, as those comments now do.

  @example
    <button type="button" aria-label="{{ 'accessibility.open_cart' | t }}">
      {% render 'icon', icon: 'cart' %}
    </button>
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign resolved_size = size | default: 16
-%}

<svg
  class="icon icon--{{ icon }} {{ class }}"
  style="--icon-size: {{ resolved_size }}px;"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="1.5"
  stroke-linecap="round"
  stroke-linejoin="round"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
>
