    {%- comment -%}
      `loader-icon.svg`, at this set's scale. The source is drawn in a 32-unit
      box and every icon here is drawn in 24, so each coordinate is three
      quarters of the original — 16 becomes 12, 28 becomes 21, 24.48 becomes
      18.36. Rescaling rather than giving this one glyph a viewBox of its own,
      because the `svg` element above is written once for the whole set: a second
      viewBox would mean a second element, and then two places for every
      decision about stroke, size and colour.

      The spokes get shorter anticlockwise from the bottom rather than fading,
      which is what makes it read as turning even at 16px and with no opacity to
      animate. The rotation is `@keyframes spin` in `assets/base.css` — the same
      one `.button__spinner` uses — applied by whatever is showing it, so this
      stays a drawing.
    {%- endcomment -%}
